<!--
    isiXhosa (xh) string overrides. Android picks this file up automatically
    whenever AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales(xh) is active -
    stringResource() calls resolve here first, falling back to the default
    values/strings.xml for any key not overridden below.

    First-pass translation, not verified by a fluent isiXhosa speaker - needs
    native-speaker review before shipping.

    Intentionally NOT overridden here (fall back to values/strings.xml):
    app_name/brand_name ("Waypoint" - a brand name), every *_glyph string
    (single-character symbols: arrows, ✎, ✕, ↺ - not language-specific
    text), and the calendar_wd_*/
    new_trip_wd_* single-letter weekday abbreviations - a single-letter
    scheme doesn't map cleanly onto isiXhosa weekday names either, so this
    needs a native speaker to pick a real abbreviation convention rather
    than a guess.
-->
